Description: Provides a client for the public API of data.gouv.fr, the French
    government's open data platform. It helps find a dataset that matches your
    interests, judge whether it is usable, download it and re-fetch the exact
    same table later in a reproducible way. You can list datasets (full-text
    search, or restricted to schema-documented ones), pull a dataset's tabular
    resources into tidy tibbles, inspect the documented variables of the data
    schema it declares, and compute summary metrics (size, number of columns,
    missing-value rate, ...). Each returned table carries a stable identifier
    so it can be re-fetched later. Requests are built on top of 'httr2'.
